  "title": "NEWLEADER ACK is sent before the DIFF-synced transactions are durable",
  "cause": "Learner.syncWithLeader (NEWLEADER) only enqueues the buffered sync proposals to the asynchronous SyncRequestProcessor via FollowerZooKeeperServer.logRequest and then writes the NEWLEADER ACK; the leader counts that ACK toward the quorum that makes it commit and serve its whole loaded history.",
  "trigger": "A transaction durable only on the re-elected leader is transferred by DIFF; the learners ACK NEWLEADER, the leader starts serving it, and the acking learners crash before their SyncRequestProcessor fsync while the old leader is unavailable.",
  "consequence": "A new leader is elected without the transaction that clients already read, and the old leader's only copy is truncated when it rejoins (lost committed write).",
  "sites": [
    "zookeeper-server/src/main/java/org/apache/zookeeper/server/quorum/Learner.java:syncWithLeader",
    "zookeeper-server/src/main/java/org/apache/zookeeper/server/quorum/FollowerZooKeeperServer.java:logRequest",
    "zookeeper-server/src/main/java/org/apache/zookeeper/server/quorum/Leader.java:waitForNewLeaderAck"
  ],
  "actions": [
    "SyncWithLeaderNewLeader",
    "LeaderBroadcast",
    "FsyncOne"
  ],
  "invariants": [
    "CommittedQuorumDurable",
    "CommittedNeverLostByLeader"
  ],
  "premises": [
    "The learner writes the NEWLEADER ACK without waiting for the SyncRequestProcessor flush of the proposals it just logged.",
    "The leader activates on a NEWLEADER ACK quorum and serves its whole loaded history.",
    "Learner process crashes (or power loss) can happen between the ACK and the asynchronous fsync."
  ],
